  "id": "menopause",
  "term": "menopause",
  "definition": "Menopause is the stage when reproductive hormone activity changes, with estrogen levels declining irregularly during the transition. In this source, it is described as naturally occurring around ages 45 to 50, with menopause before 40 termed premature and between 40 and 44 termed early, and these hormonal changes are linked to longer-term changes in cognitive function.",
